# =============================================================================
# OT/ICS Security Lab — .gitignore
# Keeps runtime state and capture data OUT of version control. The folder
# structure is preserved via committed .gitkeep marker files.
# =============================================================================

# --- FUXA runtime / HMI project state -------------------------------------
# This is live, machine-generated data written by the FUXA container. It is
# NOT source. The HMI design itself is recreated from README.md steps.
# The .gitkeep marker keeps the directory in git; everything else is ignored.
fuxa/appdata/*
!fuxa/appdata/.gitkeep

# --- Packet captures -------------------------------------------------------
# Wireshark output. Can be large and may contain lab traffic detail; never
# auto-committed. Keep the directory, ignore the captures.
captures/*
!captures/.gitkeep
*.pcap
*.pcapng

# --- OS / editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Suricata runtime logs -------------------------------------------------
# eve.json + fast.log + stats.log + suricata.log are live IDS output, not
# source. Keep the directory via .gitkeep; ignore the contents.
suricata/logs/*
!suricata/logs/.gitkeep

# --- OpenPLC Editor v4 build output ---------------------------------------
# The Editor compiles the project's ST source to MATIEC C output here on
# every Build/Compile. The build/ tree is reproducible from the committed
# project state (project.json + devices/*.json + pous/programs/main.st);
# regenerate via the Editor or pandoc-equivalent — never edited by hand.
plc/v4/editor-project/build/

# --- Cheat-sheet PDFs and source ------------------------------------------
# Markdown source + generated PDFs + supporting CSS for friends-and-family
# cheat sheets. Untracked so PDF regeneration doesn't bloat the repo with
# binary blobs. Distribute PDFs out-of-band (email / file share / GitHub
# Releases) rather than committed.
docs/cheatsheets/
